{"id": "EUVD-2026-108826", "enisaUuid": "0a3e9c31-3ee2-33a4-b840-a5aac652ab62", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: bridge: avoid recursive multicast port cleanup\n\nbr_multicast_sg_del_exclude_ports() removes automatically added STAR_EXCL\nport groups by calling br_multicast_del_pg(). For S,G entries, that\ndeletion calls back into br_multicast_sg_del_exclude_ports(), so a large\nnumber of STAR_EXCL ports consumes one kernel stack frame per port and can\nhit the stack guard page.\n\nKeep the complete port-group deletion path for cleanup, but suppress the\nS,G exclude-port cleanup while that helper is already walking the same\nentry. Normal deletion callers retain the existing behavior.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:21:31", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:21:31", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/695a5a4c69c922d9296b2d7ad5f1ce8c6858fc64", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2fb87c6025f90191516bee3ce14b42eb3e1cfed7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d109141ba14652146089ef78b32d5e4d5285ebad", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7931fb9181421953f3133b408b0f2e2b8dd68b61", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5158353121bae4f552cb677ce8c5c3ef52f93a0d"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-99031"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1d4e1ae7-04ea-3e83-9e92-11d3379d9ad8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.11"}, {"id": "1e0b638c-faea-37f9-b861-abe1500bb729", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.10"}, {"id": "1e4ba456-048f-3d14-8ee8-7e98458fa9e6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8266a0491e92d39dc9af739e8380a0daa9b8836b <5158353121bae4f552cb677ce8c5c3ef52f93a0d"}, {"id": "94524586-e785-38f3-8fd4-a5c9f908732a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "97f44142-0b72-397e-ad56-2f6e6